---
import SubpageLayout from '../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
import PhotoCredit from '../components/PhotoCredit.astro';
import Checklist from '../components/Checklist.astro';
---
<SubpageLayout
  title="Lake View Park Visitor Facilities: Toilets, Seating & Food"
  description="Lake View Park visitor facilities — restrooms, seating, food stalls, shade and parking. What to expect and what to confirm on arrival."
  path="/visitor-facilities/"
  faq={[
    { q: 'Are there toilets at Lake View Park?', a: 'Yes, toilets are provided within the park, but their exact open locations can change. Ask management for the currently open block and its route; this guide has not verified a step-free accessible toilet path.' },
    { q: 'Is there food inside the park?', a: 'CDA’s destination page describes local food stalls and tea shops. Which vendors are open, and their menus and prices, vary by day, so confirm on the day.' },
    { q: 'Is there shade and seating?', a: 'Open lawns and lakeside edges offer space to sit and rest. Shade is limited in midday summer, so plan around the heat.' },
    { q: 'What should I bring?', a: 'Water, sun protection and comfortable shoes cover most visits. For picnics, a mat and your own supplies are useful because on-site availability is not guaranteed.' },
  ]}
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Visitor facilities', href: '/visitor-facilities/' }]}
  image="/images/rawal-lake-islamabad-view.jpg"
  related={[
    { label: 'Park directory', href: '/park-directory/' },
    { label: 'Parking', href: '/parking/' },
    { label: 'Picnic guide', href: '/picnic-guide/' },
    { label: 'Accessibility', href: '/accessibility/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="space-y-8">
    <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">What to expect from the basic services at Lake View Park, and which ones are worth confirming on arrival because this guide has not verified every detail.</p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Restrooms</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Toilets are provided within the park, but their exact open locations can change. Ask management for the currently open block and its route; this guide has not verified a step-free accessible toilet path.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Seating and shade</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Open lawns and lakeside edges offer space to sit and rest. Bringing a light mat or blanket is common for picnics; shade is limited in midday summer, so plan around the heat.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Food and drink</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">CDA’s destination page describes local food stalls and tea shops. Which vendors are open, and their menus and prices, vary by day — confirm on the day rather than relying on a particular stall being present.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Parking</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Parking is available and its fee collection is outsourced per CDA’s 2023 decision. See the dedicated <a class="font-semibold text-[#a66f2d] underline" href="/parking/">parking page</a> for access and tariff notes.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Waste and bins</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Bins are provided; use them and avoid single-use plastic where you can. Keeping the lawns clean is a shared responsibility and matters for the lake’s health.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#f3ede0] p-5">
      <p class="text-sm font-black text-[#5b4a2f]">What to bring</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-[#5b4a2f]">Water, sun protection and comfortable shoes cover most visits. For picnics, a mat and your own supplies are useful because on-site availability is not guaranteed.</p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">For families</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Open lawns, lakeside edges and the children’s play areas make the park work for families, but shade is limited in midday summer and on-site food availability is not guaranteed. Bring water, sun protection and a mat, and keep children supervised near the water at all times.</p>
    </section>

    <Checklist items={[
      'Carry water and sun protection — shade is limited at midday.',
      'Wear comfortable shoes for lakeside and lawn walks.',
      'For picnics, bring a mat and your own food and water.',
      'Ask management for the currently open restroom on arrival.',
      'Use bins provided and avoid single-use plastic.',
    ]} />

    <figure>
      <img src="/images/rawal-lake-islamabad-view.jpg" width="1440" height="960" alt="Lakeside structure at Rawal Lake near Lake View Park, Islamabad" class="h-[360px] w-full rounded-[2rem] object-cover card-shadow" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption><PhotoCredit photo={3} /></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </article>
</SubpageLayout>
